DEFECT FOUND DURING run-001 (fixed immediately after)

The worker's withRetry helper retried ALL failures, including contract reverts.
A deterministic AlreadyProcessed revert was therefore logged twice as PROVER_RETRY
before being correctly classified REJECTED.

Final classification was right; the intermediate log lines in this run are wrong.
They are left in place rather than edited, since this directory records what
happened. run-002 onward uses the corrected classifier, which rethrows a revert
immediately instead of retrying it.

This is the exact conflation the state machine exists to prevent, reintroduced by
the retry wrapper added to fix a different problem.
